{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951537-2e-useful-dice-pools-\u2013-help-with-running-scenes","id":951537,"title":"[2E] Useful dice pools \u2013 Help with running scenes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-16T00:47:44-07:00","id":951537,"title":"[2E] Useful dice pools \u2013 Help with running scenes","content":"You know the feeling \u2013 you know what now actions in game are, you probably do know what Attributes + Skills to use \u2013 but you have problem with fine tuning like needed Successes, what should be Success or Dramatic Failures effects. Here is topic to help you with. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> To start, I have this a bit problematic scene. PCs are stalked by the NPC ( other mage, Guardian to be precise ) who is ordered to watch over them from a far. Here are things that need to be simulated:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>PCs uncovering \u2018tail\u2019</b> \u2013 How to play it? When to ask players to roll it? What dicepool to be used? I suspect Wits based roll ( as senses ) but do not know Skills that it could be paired with. Would only 1 Success on PCs behalf be enough? Or does it need to bit stalking NPC, like Clash of Wills-style?</li> <li><b>Losing the \u2018tail\u2019 </b>\u2013 I suspect it would play out as a bit limited to Stealth use of Chase mechanics. ( See <b>CoD </b>rulebook page 84 ) But can Chase be limited only to one Skills actions?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 08-16-2016, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T01:55:41-07:00","id":951560,"title":"","content":"1) Wits + Composure is always the default there. Though Streetwise, Survival, and Investigation could make sense depending on the location and how they're being tracked (maybe even Occult if there's a chance of spotting the tail because of any Yantras that might give them away). This should definitely be a contested roll and compare success. A well trained Guardian tail with ~8 dice to follow you undetected shouldn't be thwarted by a single success alone.<br /> <br /> 2) Chase seems tailor made of trying to lose a tail. You don't have to limit it to Stealth though. A successful Stealth roll one action could be followed by an Athletics roll to run away before the tail has time to pick up the trail after losing your for a moment. The Chase rules encourage player control here, and nothing stops them from picking the same action repeatedly if they want as long as it continues to make narrative sense. If you want to keep them using Stealth, you can make it clear Stealth will get better situational modifiers than most other Skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T02:40:47-07:00","id":951571,"title":"","content":"One more question come to me to ask:<br /> <br /> 3. <b>How to run multiple PCs Chase?</b> Like we have pursuers made by NPCs and 3-4 PCs that run from them. Or vice versa. Problem I have how I should made rolls - one for all PC and using best of them? Each PC separated? If each PC separated - how to determine who has Edge and in what order they resolve chase? And how then determine <i>when</i> someone wins?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951537-2e-useful-dice-pools-\u2013-help-with-running-scenes?p=951560#post951560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Wits + Composure is always the default there. Though Streetwise, Survival, and Investigation could make sense depending on the location and how they're being tracked (maybe even Occult if there's a chance of spotting the tail because of any Yantras that might give them away). This should definitely be a contested roll and compare success. A well trained Guardian tail with ~8 dice to follow you undetected shouldn't be thwarted by a single success alone.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Okay, but how to <i>run</i> it in the game?</b> What, I ask on start of each scene 'Roll Wits + Composure', every time? Or to run it in secret and 'play with dices' alone as ST?<br /> <br /> Also I'm not sure is this should be Extended action. Contested surely - Guardian can be better or worse than PC - but not sure it should be 'you need this and that much of successes now'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Clarification - If roll is Contested, I need one success more than oponent or five success?</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951537-2e-useful-dice-pools-\u2013-help-with-running-scenes?p=951560#post951560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Chase seems tailor made of trying to lose a tail. You don't have to limit it to Stealth though. A successful Stealth roll one action could be followed by an Athletics roll to run away before the tail has time to pick up the trail after losing your for a moment. The Chase rules encourage player control here, and nothing stops them from picking the same action repeatedly if they want as long as it continues to make narrative sense. If you want to keep them using Stealth, you can make it clear Stealth will get better situational modifiers than most other Skills.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Okay, but 'suspicious PC' should have Edge in this situation and starts rolling?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:48:40-07:00","id":951669,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theangrygm.com/five-simple-rules-for-dating-my-teenaged-skill-system/\" target=\"_blank\">This article</a> is primarily focused on D&amp;D, but it's pretty much applicable to any RPG with a pass/fail Skill system, including CofD. It's also the single most valuable piece of GMing advice I have ever read. This guy's advice is incredible if you can stomach his writing style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T13:39:47-07:00","id":951980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951537-2e-useful-dice-pools-\u2013-help-with-running-scenes?p=951571#post951571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. <b>How to run multiple PCs Chase?</b> Like we have pursuers made by NPCs and 3-4 PCs that run from them. Or vice versa. Problem I have how I should made rolls - one for all PC and using best of them? Each PC separated? If each PC separated - how to determine who has Edge and in what order they resolve chase? And how then determine <i>when</i> someone wins?</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't one answer to this.<br /> <br /> If the group is sticking together, the easiest option is to use the teamwork rules, with the lead roll getting the Edge if the players have the Edge.<br /> <br /> If the group splits up, the tail has to pick on to Chase and the other would basically just escape (unless the Guardian can track multiple individuals at once). I would recommend avoiding this if you can though, since it cuts the other players out of doing anything until the Chase is resolved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Okay, but how to <i>run</i> it in the game?</b> What, I ask on start of each scene 'Roll Wits + Composure', every time? Or to run it in secret and 'play with dices' alone as ST? </div> </div> </div>That's a group preference thing. Talk to your players about whether they like you rolling in secret for perception checks, or if they like to roll it. Some people find it annoying because if they fail they know they &quot;missed&quot; something and have to actively avoid bringing that knowledge into their decision making. Some players care more about being the one that rolls for their characters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I'm not sure is this should be Extended action. </div> </div> </div>I don't see any reason to make, &quot;do you spot the tail?&quot; an Extended action. Either you did or you didn't. You can call for rolls again if something happens to justify it without forcing an Extended roll off every time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Clarification - If roll is Contested, I need one success more than oponent or five success?</b> </div> </div> </div>Out roll your opponent. Though you'll need to make a judgement call on a tie on exactly how you want to handle it. For something like this, on a tie, I'd opt for letting the PCs have a feeling something's up, but not spot the tail, so the players can do stuff to figure out what's going on instead of just being stalked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Okay, but 'suspicious PC' should have Edge in this situation and starts rolling?</b> </div> </div> </div>Who starts with the Edge is situational. In this set up, the tail probably starts with the Edge, because they're the one's prepared for what's going on, though the players should retake it if they out roll the tail for a Chase turn. If the one side has to turn the tables on the other side, then the other side starts with the Edge; that's basically the whole point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}